room stat (`RoomStatWorker_Space`, which feeds impressiveness) scores 1.4 per standable cell and 0.5 per walkable-only cell.\n  - A quarter holding a bed scores about 21, \"rather tight\".\n  - A bare full square scores up to 113, \"quite spacious\".\n\n**What this adds to the acceptance**\n- The module is recorded in DESIGN's decisions log with the reasoning above: 11x11 walls included, pitch 10, inside 9x9.\n- Halves and quarters by centered walls, and merges by removing a shared wall, are all expressible in IR.\n- **Every room type the agent will build has a template on the grid before a game starts.** The library is the precondition for play, not a follow-on. The five existing templates are re-cut to the grid or retired: bedroom 5x7, freezer-kitchen 11x6, power-room 7x7, workshop 9x7, classroom 9x9.\n- `acee526` (exact-or-refuse placement) is still load-bearing, as comment #0 argued: a one-cell slide knocks every square after it off the grid.","files":null}]}